{0 Variables and secrets}

Use string bindings for configuration. The handler's [env] argument holds
variables and secrets as well as resource bindings. {!Workero.Env.var} returns
[Some value] for a string variable or secret. It returns [None] for a missing
name or a value that is not a string.

{1 Configure locally}

Put a non-secret variable in [wrangler.toml]:

{@toml[
[vars]
GREETING = "hello from vars"
]}

For a local secret, put [API_TOKEN=local-token] in [.dev.vars] beside
[wrangler.toml]. Keep [.dev.vars*] out of Git. Do not put secrets in [[vars]].

{1 Read a string binding}

{@ocaml[
let handler req env _ctx =
  let open Workero in
  match URL.path (Request.url req) with
  | "/greeting" -> (
      match Env.var env "GREETING" with
      | Some value -> Response.text (value ^ "\n")
      | None -> Response.text ~status:`Internal_Server_Error "GREETING is not set\n")
  | "/token" -> (
      match Env.var env "API_TOKEN" with
      | Some value ->
          Response.text (Printf.sprintf "token of %d bytes\n" (String.length value))
      | None -> Response.text ~status:`Internal_Server_Error "API_TOKEN is not set\n")
  | _ -> Response.text ~status:`Not_Found "not found\n"

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

A variable and a secret have the same string value in [env]. Do not return the
secret itself in a response.

{1 Verify locally}

Run [npx wrangler dev] in one terminal. In another terminal, run:

{@sh[
curl http://localhost:8787/greeting
curl http://localhost:8787/token
]}

The first response is [hello from vars]. With the example [.dev.vars], the
second is [token of 11 bytes]. If you omit [.dev.vars], [/token] returns
[API_TOKEN is not set] with status 500.

{1 Set a deployed secret}

Before deployment, use an authenticated Wrangler to store a secret for the
deployed Worker. Wrangler asks for the value without adding it to
[wrangler.toml]:

{@sh[
npx wrangler secret put API_TOKEN
]}

See the {{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/environment-variables/}Cloudflare variables guide},
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/secrets/}secrets guide}
and {!Workero.Env} API.
